From 90f4a90b3fee2602aac2cf3eb4f310435fdc07f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 07:31:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(resource): version resource.json with auto-migration,
 JSON schema & draft flag
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds schema versioning and a migration path for resource.json, editor
autocomplete via a generated JSON Schema, and a draft flag.

crouton-core
- `version.ts`: BASELINE/CURRENT_RESOURCE_VERSION (both 1 — no-op until a real
  shape change bumps CURRENT and adds a step).
- `migrations/`: pure, testable engine (`runResourceMigrations`) operating on
  raw JSON with a contiguous single-step chain; path/step error types.
- `ResourceJsonShape`: add `$schema`, `schemaVersion`, `draft`; stamp
  schemaVersion in the transform.
- `scripts/gen-resource-schema.mjs` + tsup `onSuccess`: generate
  resource.schema.json from the Shape (io:input) into dist (shipped) and a
  committed copy; CI drift-check in merge-request.yml.

crouton-api
- `MigrateResourceJson.ts`: dev-only auto-migrate-on-load (rewrites file);
  out-of-date/newer files outside dev are reported, never rewritten;
  unparseable files pass through to the existing reader.
- loader: migrate hook + draft exclusion; `resource-load-report.registry.ts`
  for migrated/draft notices; errors registry carries version/expectedVersion.
- status: resources report version; drafts show as valid-but-not-served;
  migration failures carry expectedVersion.

crouton-vue
- StatusView: version badge, amber "needs migration", gray "draft" row.

crouton-codegen / cli
- `withResourceHeader` stamps $schema + schemaVersion (+ draft) on generated
  files; new resources default to draft:true, `--no-draft` opts out.

Tests: migration engine, loader draft/stale, status draft/version, codegen header.

